course: dictionary
lesson: 1479
title: Words for buildings and places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cathedral is a very large and important Christian church. It is the main church of an area, and it is led by a bishop. You will meet the word in stories, history books and on maps, so it is worth knowing well.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Lincoln Cathedral in England was probably the tallest building in the world for about 200 years» tells you a cathedral is huge. «Galileo noticed this watching a swinging lamp in a cathedral» tells you it is a place where people go inside.
explain: Try the swap check. Put "church" in place of "cathedral" in «Italy is younger than her favourite cathedral». The sentence still makes sense, because a cathedral is a kind of church. The word cathedral just tells you it is a bigger and more important one.
fact: A cathedral is a very large and important Christian church.
fact: A cathedral is the main church of an area, and it is led by a bishop.
fact: Cathedrals took many years to build, with tall towers, spires and stained-glass windows.
fact: «A whisper can travel round a curved wall in a whispering gallery, such as the famous one in St Paul's Cathedral in London.»
fact: Famous cathedrals include St Paul's, Canterbury, Notre-Dame and St Patrick's.
exercise: «Lincoln Cathedral in England was probably the tallest building in the world for about 200 years.» What is a cathedral? | A tall tree in a park | A kind of bird that hunts pigeons | *A very large and important Christian church | A small shop that sells bread
exercise: «Galileo noticed this watching a swinging lamp in a cathedral.» Where did Galileo watch the lamp? | In a forest | *In a cathedral | In a shop | On a boat
exercise: Cathedrals often have tall towers with a pointed top. Which word means that pointed top? | pulse | *spire | crumb | sparrow
test: «A whisper can travel round a curved wall in a whispering gallery.» Where can a whisper travel round a curved wall? | In a school playground | In a noisy bus | *In a whispering gallery | In a cave under the sea
test: What is the main church of an area, led by a bishop, called? | A supermarket | A castle | *A cathedral | A library
exam: «Many countries are young: Giulia's nonna jokes that Italy is younger than her favourite cathedral.» Which is true about a cathedral? | It is a type of spider | It is a kind of sweet | It is a small room inside a house | *It is a very large and important Christian church
